  "extended_at": "2026-08-23T06:58:55.440008+00:00",
  "extended_by": "energy-sprint/packs/extend_packs.py",
  "notes": "Schneider ION carries units as a PREFIX (kWh_Del, kVAR_Tot). No suffix rule can read that, which is why every one of these must be declared per tag rather than inferred.",
  "rationale": "The pack maps PF and kVAR tags but declares no unit for either, so both fell through the converter's 'no source unit' path untouched. That was survivable only because ION already reports kVAR in kVAR \u2014 until 2026-08-22 the converter had no `var` unit at all, so any meter reporting raw vars would have been stored 1000x high with no flag. Units are now declared explicitly.\n\nAlso adds the ION Modbus register spellings, which differ from the PowerLogic labels already present.",
  "registry_field_count": 394,
  "tier": "vendor_doc"
 },
